ntry i (of hash h, the last entry) at the end of its hash's chain."] [98 1 "// indexForget takes entry i (of hash h, the last entry) out of its hash's chain."] [135 1 "// AsDict is asDict, exported for the other files."] [138 1 "// Len is the number of items."] [165 1 "// matches is whether entry i's key (of the hash looked up) is key: the same object, the same str, else __eq__."] [185 3 "// directly, not through the slot: the types' dictionaries are filled by init functions that may"] [186 3 "// run before str's sets its slots"] [196 1 "// Get is d[key], nil when absent."] [209 1 "// Set is d[key] = v."] [234 1 "// insertNew appends key (of hash h, not in the dict) with value v."] [260 1 "// Delete removes key; false when absent."] [270 50 "// a hole; its chain link kept"] [279 1 "// Clear empties the dict."] [288 1 "// GetStr and SetStr are Get and Set with a str key (the namespaces')."] [296 1 "// nameStr is the interned str of a name GetStr and SetStr look up (attribute and special names), a code's co_names"] [297 1 "// or an identifier-like str constant, so each is made and hashed once: sys.intern's table (internTable), as CPython"] [298 1 "// interns them all in one (queue 211; before it a table of its own, so `sys.intern(s) is name` could fail). At most"] [299 1 "// nameStrsMax names are added to it this way."] [316 1 "// Items calls f on each item in order until it returns false."] [326 1 "// Keys is the keys in order."] [333 1 "// Copy is a shallow copy."] [347 1 "// Update is dict.update(o): a mapping's items (keys() and []), or an iterable of pairs."] [350 3 "// the other dict's entries by position, its change by a key's __eq__ an error (dict_merge's check of"] [351 3 "// dk_nentries; queue 203: test_merge_and_mutate)"] [381 3 "// PySequence_Fast(x, \"object is not iterable\"), its TypeError given the note (dict_merge_from_seq2; queue 203:"] [382 3 "// test_update_type_error)"] [417 16 "// a reverse iterator: i counts the entries left, from the last"] [418 16 "// the items still expected (di->len)"] [419 16 "// the dict's compactions when made"] [460 1 "// dictNew is dict(), dict(mapping or iterable, **kwargs)."] [591 4 "// the size checked, the iteration ended past the entries of a dict refilled since, and the keys changed"] [592 4 "// when it meets an item it did not expect (dictiter_iternextkey_lock_held, dictreviter_iter_lock_held;"] [593 4 "// queue 203: test_reversed_dict_after_clear_and_restore; before it any change of the keys was one)"] [598 4 "// compacted since (CPython's resize, at other moments): the positions lost, the keys changed"] [630 3 "// __reduce__ is dictiter_reduce: (iter, (list,)), the list the items a copy of the iterator would give,"] [631 3 "// the iterator itself not advanced (queue 211: test_dict's six *iterator_pickling tests)"] [674 2 "// a view's mapping: a mappingproxy of its dict (dictview_mapping; queue 203: test_views_mapping)"] [706 1 "// dictViewCompare is dictview_richcompare: the sizes, then every item of one in the other by the other's"] [707 1 "// containment (an items view's: the key looked up, the values compared), no set made (queue 203: an unhashable"] [708 1 "// value compared, test_errors_in_view_containment_check)."] [790 1 "// dictMissing is d[k] on a dict subclass with __missing__: the method called with the key."] [806 1 "// newDictSubclass makes an instance of a dict subclass; PY5c sets it (by default the base value: PY5c wraps it)."] [843 3 "// the key hashed and looked up once (dict_setdefault_ref; queue 203: test_setdefault_atomic)"] [889 5 "// the slot leaves the index too: a later key of its hash looked up entries[i] past the end"] [890 5 "// (PY6e's REQUEST: test_os's mapping tests popitem then set)"] [891 5 "// the popped entry and the holes after it leave the index too: a later key appended at their"] [892 5 "// positions is found by its own chain only"] [929 2 "// dict.fromkeys, a class method (dict_fromkeys: cls() filled by its __setitem__; PY7: it was a plain built-in,"] [930 2 "// bound to an instance, d.fromkeys(keys) iterated d)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[105 28] [129 25] [149 17] [149 47] [156 35] [171 22] [172 25] [184 24] [305 31] [318 12] [318 32] [329 55] [349 23] [353 13] [353 20] [356 50] [366 44] [385 27] [391 29] [445 23] [448 23] [468 29] [473 39] [482 49] [492 42] [527 25] [532 25] [565 49] [574 50] [633 48] [710 27] [711 23] [739 28] [748 28] [754 28] [763 22] [774 27] [775 26] [796 33] [814 54] [824 40] [840 47] [864 40] [882 49] [886 30] [886 38] [917 47] [924 46] [935 24]]} (go/file "dict.go" :imports [


